No. It has ","decorations":[]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"no official status","decorations":[{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700}]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" and is not a holiday anyw here.","decorations":[]}}],"style":{"paddingTop":"0px","paddingBottom":"10px"},"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"JUSTIFY","lineHeight":"1.5"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"0ygls212","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Q. What is the difference between Brothers Day and Siblings Day?","decorations":[{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700}]}}],"style":{"paddingTop":"0px","paddingBottom":"10px"},"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"JUSTIFY","lineHeight":"1.5"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"53243214","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"A. Brothers Day is 24 May","decorations":[{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700}]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" and is about brothers. ","decorations":[]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"National Siblings Day is 10 April","decorations":[{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700}]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" and covers all siblings, brothers and sisters together.","decorations":[]}}],"style":{"paddingTop":"0px","paddingBottom":"10px"},"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"JUSTIFY","lineHeight":"1.5"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"02ofy219","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Q. Can I celebrate Brothers Day with a close friend?","decorations":[{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700}]}}],"style":{"paddingTop":"0px","paddingBottom":"10px"},"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"JUSTIFY","lineHeight":"1.5"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"4l3d7221","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"A.","decorations":[{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700}]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" Yes. The day is commonly marked with ","decorations":[]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"cousins, brothers in law and friends","decorations":[{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700}]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" who are treated as brothers, not only with biological siblings.","decorations":[]}}],"style":{"paddingTop":"0px","paddingBottom":"10px"},"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"JUSTIFY","lineHeight":"1.5"}}}],"documentStyle":{}},"contentText":"National Brothers Day is observed on 24 May every year, which in 2027 falls on a Monday. Unlike Sisters Day, the date is fixed rather than tied to a weekday. It was created by C. Daniel Rhodes of Alabama in 2005, making it one of the few informal observances of this kind with a traceable origin. It has no official status, is not a public holiday anywhere, and is marked mostly with messages, posts and small gifts. National Brothers Day dates Year Date Day 2026 24 May 2026 Sunday (already passed) 2027 24 May 2027 Monday 2028 24 May 2028 Wednesday 2029 24 May 2029 Thursday Brothers Day, Siblings Day, Raksha Bandhan and Bhai Dooj Four different occasions, regularly mixed up. The difference is who they are between and where they come from. Occasion When What it marks National Brothers Day 24 May, fixed The bond between brothers. Created by C. Daniel Rhodes in 2005. Informal, no rituals. National Siblings Day 10 April, fixed All siblings. Founded by Claudia Evart in 1995. Raksha Bandhan Shravana Purnima, July or August A sister ties a rakhi and the brother pledges protection. A traditional Indian festival. Bhai Dooj Two days after Diwali A sister applies a tilak and the brother gives a gift. Also called Bhai Phota or Bhau Beej.   The simplest way to keep them apart: Brothers Day is brother to brother. Raksha Bandhan and Bhai Dooj are brother and sister. Wishes and messages for your brother Short and direct •       Happy Brothers Day to the one who has covered for me more times than either of us will admit. •       First rival, permanent teammate. Happy Brothers Day. •       Thanks for the arguments and everything after them. Happy Brothers Day. •       You are the one call I know will always be picked up. Happy Brothers Day. For an older brother •       You cleared the path and then pretended it was easy. Thank you. •       Everything I figured out early, I figured out because you went first. For a younger brother •       You have overtaken me in more ways than I want to list. Proud of you. •       Still the kid I taught to ride a bike, still the person I go to for advice. For a brother who lives away •       Different time zones, same brother. Happy Brothers Day. •       The distance is the only thing about this that I would change. For a friend who is like a brother •       Not blood, still family. Happy Brothers Day. •       You earned the title. Happy Brothers Day. Gift ideas for Brothers Day •       Something for a hobby he already has, rather than something meant to start a new one. •       A printed photo or a small album from a trip you took together. •       Tickets to something, a match, a gig, a film, so the gift is time rather than an object. •       An upgrade to something he uses daily and has not bothered replacing. •       A letter, if the two of you never talk seriously. Awkward to write, hard to throw away. •       For a brother living away, food or a product from home that he cannot easily get. How to mark the day if you are not the sentimental type Not everybody wants a card. A call with no occasion attached is often the version that actually lands. Other options that take under an hour: send an old photo with no caption, settle a debt neither of you has mentioned, or turn up. The day exists as a prompt, not a script, and there is no wrong way to use it. Frequently asked questions about National Brothers Day Q. When is National Brothers Day 2027? A. Monday, 24 May 2027. The date is fixed at 24 May each year, so only the weekday changes. Q. Who started National Brothers Day? A. C. Daniel Rhodes of Alabama, in 2005. It is an informal observance and has never been officially recognised by any government. Q. Is National Brothers Day the same as Raksha Bandhan? A. No. Raksha Bandhan is a traditional Indian festival between a brother and sister, marked with a rakhi. National Brothers Day is a modern informal day celebrating brothers, with no rituals. Q. Is National Brothers Day a public holiday in India? A. No. It has no official status and is not a holiday anyw here. Q. What is the difference between Brothers Day and Siblings Day? A. Brothers Day is 24 May and is about brothers. National Siblings Day is 10 April and covers all siblings, brothers and sisters together. Q. Can I celebrate Brothers Day with a close friend? A. Yes. The day is commonly marked with cousins, brothers in law and friends who are treated as brothers, not only with biological siblings."}